          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Conflicts we found</h3>
          <p>
            Overseas dealer listings are less consistent. One gives a 3.0 HP drive, and an Australian listing gives an
            assembled weight of 392 lb. On 220 V supplies the top speed is 13.8 mph, which explains some listings' higher
            figures. We have used Vision's and the US dealer's matching figures on the cards.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Price and warranty</h3>
          <p>
            Vision publishes no prices. Fitness Supply listed the T600E at $8,799 on 5 November 2026. A US T600ENT listing
            seen in search results showed the same figure; earlier listings put the LED T600 at about $5,400 in the US and
            $4,699 in Canada, but we could not confirm those on the day. Warranty depends on the dealer and on how the
            treadmill is used: Fitness Supply's commercial-use terms were 7 years on the frame, 5 on the motor and parts,
            2 on labour and 90 days on wear items, and another retailer page in search results showed a lifetime frame,
            5-year motor and 2-year labour term, which may be the residential version. Ask the dealer for the warranty in
            writing, for home use, before you buy.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Putting one in a home</h3>
          <p>
            Vision lists a NEMA 5-15 plug for 100-120 V supplies, the ordinary household plug shape, so a 20-amp
            circuit may not be required; ask the dealer whether a dedicated circuit is recommended. The bigger issues are
            size and weight: 85 inches long, 65 inches high and 408 lb, with no fold. Our guide to putting a
            <a href="/gym-treadmill-for-home/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">gym treadmill in a home</a>
            covers floors, stairs and access routes.
          </p>
